// PARAM: --analysis interval --context entry-state
// Same program as known-imprecision/01-two_call_sites_same_procedure.vimp,
// under entry-state context sensitivity instead of the default flat
// analysis. There, both calls to square share ONE flow-insensitive
// activation, so square's summary is the join over every call site --
// combine reads back join([9,9], [16,16]) = [9,16] at both checks, and
// neither can be proved. Here, each call is keyed by its own entered
// argument value ([9,9] vs [16,16] respectively), so square is analyzed
// once per distinct entry-state context instead of joined into one shared
// summary -- an observable precision benefit of #108's context analysis
// over the flat default, not a different claim about the concrete program
// (both checks are true for the same reason in both files: 3*3=9,
// 4*4=16).
void square(n) {
  return n * n
}
void main() {
  a := square(3);
  b := square(4);
  __voblint_check(a == 9); // PROVED
  __voblint_check(b == 16) // PROVED
}
